cripRef>Eze 27:12,19; Re 18:12</scripRef><br /><br />- Great quantity of, provided for the temple<br /><scripRef>1Ch 22:3,14,16; 29:2</scripRef><br /><br />- Taken in war, often dedicated to God<br /><scripRef>Jos 6:19,24</scripRef><br /><br />- Mode of purifying, taken in war<br /><scripRef>Nu 31:21-23</scripRef><br /><br />- Miraculously made to swim<br /><scripRef>2Ki 6:6</scripRef><br /><br />- Illustrative<br />. Of strength<br /><scripRef>Da 2:33,40</scripRef><br /><br />. Of stubbornness<br /><scripRef>Isa 48:4</scripRef><br /><br />. Of severe affliction<br /><scripRef>De 4:20; Ps 107:10</scripRef><br /><br />. Of a hard barren soil<br /><scripRef>De 28:23</scripRef><br /><br />. Of severe exercise of power<br /><scripRef>Ps 2:9; Re 2:27</scripRef><br /><br />. (Seared with,) of insensibility of conscience<br /><scripRef>1Ti 4:2</scripRef>

